Setting up a Python development environment in Emacs with Eglot and python-lsp-server (pylsp) requires telling the language server which plugins to run and which ones to ignore. While you can set eglot-workspace-configuration globally, doing so forces every Python project you open using Emacs to use the same toolchain and formatting rules. Placing the configuration in a .dir-locals.el file applies these Emacs buffer settings and Eglot workspace settings to files within the project's directory tree. The indentation settings and fill-column can be chosen to match the conventions configured in pyproject.toml, while Ruff reads its own configuration from that file when applicable. &#8230; <a href="https://www.jamescherti.com/emacs-eglot-python-dir-locals-el-and-pylsp/">Continue reading <span class="meta-nav">&#8594;</span></a>